WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:06.310
We are now learning about the existence of
a literal, not proverbial pandemic playbook

00:00:06.310 --> 00:00:10.450
that Donald Trump and the White House had
in their possession.

00:00:10.450 --> 00:00:15.420
They'd had it for years and they just ignored
it as they continued to insist Corona virus

00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:18.269
is no big deal and now everything's just fine.

00:00:18.269 --> 00:00:23.100
This is a color coded 69 page long playbook.

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:25.869
It's a manual for fighting pandemics.

00:00:25.869 --> 00:00:28.920
If they simply followed it, they didn't have
to come up with anything new.

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:30.150
They didn't have to.

00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:31.619
The information was all right there.

00:00:31.619 --> 00:00:36.880
They simply followed the 69 page document
that they had all along that they were briefed

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:40.570
on in twenty seventeen by the outgoing Obama
administration.

00:00:40.570 --> 00:00:43.010
Think about how much better off we would all
be right now.

00:00:43.010 --> 00:00:46.900
Think about how many fewer deaths we would
be on target to have.

00:00:46.900 --> 00:00:54.850
The playbook dates to 2016 and the playbook
was created because in 2014/15 we had Ebola.

00:00:54.850 --> 00:00:56.340
Lessons were learned.

00:00:56.340 --> 00:00:58.460
So a playbook was put together.

00:00:58.460 --> 00:01:00.210
This is called iteration.

00:01:00.210 --> 00:01:01.550
It's called learning.

00:01:01.550 --> 00:01:03.670
The playbook was made in 2016.

00:01:03.670 --> 00:01:07.130
It was turned over to the Trump administration
in 2017.

00:01:07.130 --> 00:01:09.609
They were briefed on the playbook in 2017.

00:01:09.609 --> 00:01:13.450
Then, of course, Donald Trump disbanded the
pandemic response team.

00:01:13.450 --> 00:01:16.380
We know where we are today as a result of
that.

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:22.109
And as you all probably realize by now, pandemics
are an issue of national security.

00:01:22.109 --> 00:01:24.700
This is a national security document.

00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:30.780
It's the National Security Council's pandemic
playbook, 69 pages.

00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:34.060
And it was just ignored, simply ignored, like
it doesn't exist.

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:36.960
And this is another interesting thing.

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:42.299
On Monday, I gave a list of what should Trump
have done and when should he have done it?

00:01:42.299 --> 00:01:47.030
Now, at the time, I wasn't aware of this playbook,
but many of the things I mentioned, including

00:01:47.030 --> 00:01:50.740
the timelines, are literally in this playbook
right at the start.

00:01:50.740 --> 00:01:55.979
So one of the things I said was months ago,
that's when the government needs to start

00:01:55.979 --> 00:02:01.869
obtaining, securing and distributing personal
protective equipment, including masks and

00:02:01.869 --> 00:02:05.799
gloves and looking at getting the ventilators
to where they need to be.

00:02:05.799 --> 00:02:12.470
The playbook says one of the things you do
at the first sign of the pandemic is you ask,

00:02:12.470 --> 00:02:17.370
is there sufficient PPE, personal protective
equipment for health care workers who are

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:19.430
providing medical care?

00:02:19.430 --> 00:02:21.500
If the answer is no.

00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:27.599
Should the strategic national stockpile be
released to states? Trump started talking

00:02:27.599 --> 00:02:30.470
about this eight days ago, nine days ago.

00:02:30.470 --> 00:02:35.170
Maybe the playbook says, just like I said
on Monday, that should have been done in January

00:02:35.170 --> 00:02:36.550
at the absolute latest.

00:02:36.550 --> 00:02:37.810
Trump simply didn't do it.

00:02:37.810 --> 00:02:38.810
It was in the playbook.

00:02:38.810 --> 00:02:43.830
It was in the document that they were given
the funding stuff, the checks and and the

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:44.830
stimulus.

00:02:44.830 --> 00:02:50.019
I said on Monday, you need to start negotiating
and planning the bailout early so that the

00:02:50.019 --> 00:02:52.580
money can actually get to people when they
need it.

00:02:52.580 --> 00:02:54.569
We are now almost in April.

00:02:54.569 --> 00:03:00.000
With luck, people will get their twelve hundred
dollar checks in three weeks and that's only

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:04.440
half because remember, you'll get a direct
deposit in roughly three weeks, assuming it

00:03:04.440 --> 00:03:06.700
passes the House later today.

00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:13.650
If you file taxes in 2018 or 2019, filed your
2018 or 2019 taxes and receive the refund

00:03:13.650 --> 00:03:18.560
via direct deposit, that's how you'll get
your check, your twelve hundred bucks in three

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:19.560
weeks.

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:23.819
The other half is unlikely to get their twelve
hundred bucks for an additional three to five

00:03:23.819 --> 00:03:25.450
weeks beyond that.

00:03:25.450 --> 00:03:31.520
The playbook says plan in advance with legislators
to have the money ready.

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:32.600
They didn't do it.

00:03:32.600 --> 00:03:38.180
It's actually shocking that the advice is
so obvious that even I who know nothing about

00:03:38.180 --> 00:03:39.180
this stuff.

00:03:39.180 --> 00:03:43.659
I was able to put together a list of stuff
that should have been done that we now know

00:03:43.659 --> 00:03:47.480
mirrors much of what was in this pandemic
response playbook.

00:03:47.480 --> 00:03:48.799
And they had the playbook.

00:03:48.799 --> 00:03:50.540
They didn't have to do the thinking part.

00:03:50.540 --> 00:03:52.730
They just had to do the doing part.

00:03:52.730 --> 00:03:53.829
And they didn't do it.

00:03:53.829 --> 00:03:59.090
They had a physical playbook with instructions
and they ignored all of it.

00:03:59.090 --> 00:04:03.109
And what we now I mean, illicit data, there's
always these questions if you don't start

00:04:03.109 --> 00:04:06.180
assigning blame in the middle of stuff, but
at the same time, if you think you need someone

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:09.390
else leading the cause, you do have to assign
blame.

00:04:09.390 --> 00:04:12.640
When this is all said and done, is anybody
going to be held accountable?

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:18.489
And what I mean by that is when the death
toll stops and when we get beyond this, which

00:04:18.489 --> 00:04:23.889
hopefully will be as soon as humanly possible,
are there going to be consequences or is Trump

00:04:23.889 --> 00:04:25.610
going to get himself another four years?

00:04:25.610 --> 00:04:29.800
Because as we've talked about yesterday and
earlier in the week, the approval rating for

00:04:29.800 --> 00:04:31.080
Trump is up.

00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:36.490
The portion of the population satisfied with
his handling of this is up.

00:04:36.490 --> 00:04:43.360
And what I've really come to realize during
this Corona virus pandemic is I really prefer

00:04:43.360 --> 00:04:48.699
my dystopias to be only in the fiction books
that I'm reading and not in reality.

00:04:48.699 --> 00:04:53.050
I love dystopian science fiction, and yet
I'm finding myself struggling to read any

00:04:53.050 --> 00:05:36.810
of it right now because it's all feeling just

00:05:36.810 --> 00:06:19.540
a little bit too real.

